  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The temperature of object P is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\\:{}^{\\circ}\\textup{C}\"></span> and the temperature of object Q is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"600\\:{}^{\\circ}\\textup{C}\"></span>. The peak wavelength emitted by object P is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span>. </p>\n<p>What is the best estimate for the peak wavelength emitted by object Q?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda}{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2 \\lambda\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3 \\lambda\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
